26:["$","aside",null,{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-500/5 p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground","role":"note","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-medium text-foreground","children":"Educational only — not investment advice"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","children":"ContentVerse India publishes general financial education. Nothing here is a buy/sell recommendation, portfolio advice, or a substitute for a SEBI-registered adviser. Markets involve risk; verify figures with your broker, bank, or official filings."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs","children":"Last reviewed: September 2026. Confirm live rules on official portals."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-xs","children":["Useful official sources",":"," ",[["$","span","https://www.sebi.gov.in/",{"children":[null,["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"SEBI"}]]}],["$","span","https://www.rbi.org.in/",{"children":[" · ",["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.rbi.org.in/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"RBI"}]]}],["$","span","https://www.nseindia.com/",{"children":[" · ",["$","$L8",null,{"href":"https://www.nseindia.com/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"text-primary hover:underline","children":"NSE"}]]}]]]}]]}]
27:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-8 xl:flex-row xl:items-start","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-10","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl font-semibold","children":["How to use ","FD Calculator"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"A Fixed Deposit (FD) lets you lock a lump sum with a bank or company for a fixed period at a fixed interest rate. This FD calculator shows the maturity amount and the interest you will earn, using quarterly compounding — the method most Indian banks use for cumulative deposits. Use it to compare offers between banks, choose a tenure and plan cash flows before you open a deposit."}]]}],[["$","div","How to use the FD calculator",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How to use the FD calculator"}],[["$","p","Enter the deposit amount, the annual interest ra",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Enter the deposit amount, the annual interest rate offered and the tenure in years. The tool applies the compound-interest formula and shows the interest earned and the maturity value. Run the same amount at two or three different rates to see how a small rate difference changes the final sum."}],["$","p","Use the rate printed in the bank’s current rate ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Use the rate printed in the bank’s current rate card for your exact tenure and category. Senior-citizen rates are usually 0.25–0.50 percentage points higher than regular rates, so enter the right one for the depositor."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Principal: the amount you deposit once at the start",{"children":"Principal: the amount you deposit once at the start"}],["$","li","Rate: the annual rate quoted by the bank for your tenure",{"children":"Rate: the annual rate quoted by the bank for your tenure"}],["$","li","Tenure: years until maturity; many banks also offer odd-day tenures",{"children":"Tenure: years until maturity; many banks also offer odd-day tenures"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex justify-center py-2","children":["$","aside",null,{"aria-label":"Advertisement","data-cv-ad-zone":"mrec","className":"mx-auto flex w-fit max-w-full flex-col items-center","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1.5 text-center text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground/70","children":"Ad"}],["$","$L2c",null,{"slotKey":"inArticle","width":300,"height":250}]]}]}]]}],["$","div","How FD interest is calculated",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How FD interest is calculated"}],[["$","p","For a cumulative FD the maturity amount is A = P",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"For a cumulative FD the maturity amount is A = P × (1 + r ÷ n)^(n × t), where r is the annual rate, n is the number of compounding periods per year and t is the time in years. Banks in India typically compound quarterly, so n = 4. The calculator uses this default."}],["$","p","In a non-cumulative FD the bank pays interest ou",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"In a non-cumulative FD the bank pays interest out monthly, quarterly or yearly and your principal stays the same. That suits people who need regular income, but the total return is lower than a cumulative FD of the same rate, because the interest is not reinvested."}]],null,null]}],"$L2d","$L2e"]]}],"$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33"]}],"$L34"]}]
